Describe a numerical integration problem and explain which integration
method you would use to solve this problem, keeping in mind the balance between accuracy
and computation time. Justify your choice

It depends on the function and acceptable error; when not expressed in closed-form numerical integration relys on approximation.I would prefer Simpsons on the simplicity of control with slicing/step to better processing time and error rate. The variation between error and true value is reduced on increased slice/steps but becomes marginal after 100 in "most" cases until it hits the limit of python. 
